Looking closely at the image aed51eaf-bc26-44d7-8a85-96414a4a1c07, the absolute root cause of the visual overflow becomes crystal clear.
The elements are visually breaking out because of an extreme layout mismatch between your **parent component padding** and your **nested component widths**.
Inside VoucherAuthorization, you have your action screen content nested inside a multi-layered structure where fixed widths or excessive paddings are causing a layout spill:
 1. actionScreenBox applies **p: 5** (massive internal padding).
 2. actionCard forces a rigid width constraints on top of it (**width: "100%", maxWidth: 650**).
 3. The internal contents like the Stack are fighting for space inside those double-padded constraints, completely shattering the layout boundaries.
## The Fix: Complete Structural Overhaul
To eliminate this spacing issue entirely, we need to balance the layout weights. We will strip away the conflicting padding, drop the fixed widths, convert the Stack wrapper to a standard fluid Grid, and set explicit cell breakpoints.
### 1. The React Component Replacement
Locate the code block under {actionSelection === "REJECTED" ? ( ... ) : ( inside your conditional routing section, and replace the Stack structure with this highly responsive, grid-confined structure:
